@ConsoleApp2.Api_HostAddress = http://localhost:5088

### API liveness only: 200 {"status":"Healthy"}; no database or LLM calls.
GET {{ConsoleApp2.Api_HostAddress}}/health

### Chat-model probe: no PostgreSQL or embeddings. Calls the configured LLM (may incur cost).
### 200 with nonempty model text; 503 unavailable/empty; 504 after a 30-second deadline.
### Use sparingly on a trusted network; this is not database or knowledge-index readiness.
GET {{ConsoleApp2.Api_HostAddress}}/health/llm

### Index JSON knowledge (Development environment and User Secrets required):
### dotnet run --project Cyclus.Claim\LLM.Api\LLMChat.Api.csproj -- --index-knowledge
### Re-run after changing articles or embedding models; all embeddings are regenerated.
### Search results are nearest neighbors, not necessarily relevant answers.
POST {{ConsoleApp2.Api_HostAddress}}/knowledge/search
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "question": "How do I reset a forgotten password in Cyclus?"
}

### Test the configured embedding model with non-sensitive text
POST {{ConsoleApp2.Api_HostAddress}}/embeddings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "text": "How do I reset a forgotten password in Cyclus?"
}

### Chat uses PostgreSQL vector search for application knowledge; no caller ragContext is required.
### KnowledgeSearch:MinimumSimilarity defaults to 0.6 and should be tuned against representative questions.
### The database must be indexed with the configured embedding model before running chat.
POST {{ConsoleApp2.Api_HostAddress}}/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "message": "How do I reset a forgotten password in Cyclus?",
  "maxOutputTokens": 1000
}

### Procedural questions use knowledge, not the live claim-status action
POST {{ConsoleApp2.Api_HostAddress}}/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "message": "How do I check claim status in Cyclus?",
  "availableTools": ["prepare_outlook_email", "get_claim_status"],
  "maxOutputTokens": 1000
}

### Unverified procedures must not invent screens or buttons
POST {{ConsoleApp2.Api_HostAddress}}/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "message": "How do I launch a spacecraft in Cyclus?",
  "maxOutputTokens": 1000
}

###

POST {{ConsoleApp2.Api_HostAddress}}/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "message": "Can you summarize this thread in 3 bullets?",
  "modelName": "gpt-oss-120b",
  "systemPrompt": "You are a concise enterprise assistant.",
  "history": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "What is our security requirement?"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Policy v3 requires MFA for all admin users."
    }
  ],
  "ragContext": [
    "Policy v3 requires MFA for all admin users.",
    "Support hours are 9 AM to 6 PM GST, Sunday to Thursday."
  ],
  "maxOutputTokens": 300,
  "includeLogProbabilities": false,
  "topLogProbabilityCount": 0,
  "stopSequences": [
    "\n\nEND"
  ]
}

###

### Prepare an Outlook draft (requires a model that supports function calling)
POST {{ConsoleApp2.Api_HostAddress}}/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "message": "Help me email alex@example.com. Subject: Tomorrow's meeting. Message: Hi Alex, can we meet tomorrow at 10 AM?",
  "autoDetectEmailDrafts": true,
  "maxOutputTokens": 1200
}

### Sending a selected assistant-written summary must return emailDraft, not copy/paste prose
POST {{ConsoleApp2.Api_HostAddress}}/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "message": "Yes, send it.",
  "availableTools": ["prepare_outlook_email", "get_claim_status"],
  "history": [
    { "role": "user", "content": "Write a quick RCM summary." },
    { "role": "assistant", "content": "RCM manages eligibility, claims, payments and denials to improve cash flow." },
    { "role": "user", "content": "Email this summary to alex@example.com with subject hello world." },
    { "role": "assistant", "content": "I cannot send email directly. I can prepare the summary as an email to alex@example.com with subject hello world." }
  ],
  "maxOutputTokens": 1200
}

### Gather missing email details instead of creating an incomplete action
POST {{ConsoleApp2.Api_HostAddress}}/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "message": "I want to email someone",
  "autoDetectEmailDrafts": true,
  "maxOutputTokens": 1200
}

### An unrelated question does not enable the email tool
POST {{ConsoleApp2.Api_HostAddress}}/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "message": "What is 2 + 2?",
  "autoDetectEmailDrafts": true,
  "history": [
    { "role": "user", "content": "Help me draft an email." },
    { "role": "assistant", "content": "Who should receive it?" }
  ],
  "maxOutputTokens": 1200
}

### Request a claim status lookup (the trusted Claims backend executes it)
POST {{ConsoleApp2.Api_HostAddress}}/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "message": "What is the status of Claim ID 123?",
  "availableTools": ["prepare_outlook_email", "get_claim_status"],
  "maxOutputTokens": 1200
}

### Ask for a missing Claim ID
POST {{ConsoleApp2.Api_HostAddress}}/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "message": "Check a claim's status",
  "availableTools": ["get_claim_status"],
  "maxOutputTokens": 1200
}

### Continue claim lookup using conversation context
POST {{ConsoleApp2.Api_HostAddress}}/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "message": "123",
  "history": [
    { "role": "user", "content": "Check a claim's status" },
    { "role": "assistant", "content": "Please provide the Claim ID." }
  ],
  "availableTools": ["get_claim_status"],
  "maxOutputTokens": 1200
}

### A historical permission denial must not prevent a fresh lookup
POST {{ConsoleApp2.Api_HostAddress}}/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "message": "I signed in again, try again",
  "history": [
    { "role": "user", "content": "Check Claim ID 4980304" },
    { "role": "assistant", "content": "You do not have permission to check this claim's status. Sign in again if your session has expired." }
  ],
  "availableTools": ["get_claim_status"],
  "maxOutputTokens": 1200
}
